{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792006035,"nonce":"PlDjtZfo2V3Lc6KM1rDwvzUxvf4=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABcCamcg","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/168#issuecomment-6176548466"},"message":"With cuDSS disabled (`cudss_ffi.available = lambda: False`) the same welded solve on the GPU fails differently: `ValueError: Out shape is mismatched [executable_name='jit_true_divide']` from the preconditioner's host callback (`_precond` -\u003e `pure_callback(_holder_solve, shape_out, r, vmap_method=\"expand_dims\")`), so the fallback path is broken on the GPU as well -- `_host_or_device_lu` presumably returns a different shape or dtype than `shape_out` declares when it runs on the device. On the CPU both paths converge.","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1792515599,"nonce":"BzllWCGoZ9yXQl80cjzG5DmTNlg=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABd0wDAw","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/168#issuecomment-6296437507"},"message":"Root cause of the \"Out shape is mismatched\" on the host-callback path (cuDSS custom call disabled, cupy present):\n\n`_DeviceLU.solve` assumes ONE right-hand side, but `_batched_lu` hands it a batch: `rhs` has shape `(n, k)`.\nTwo things then break:\n\n- `pre * np.asarray(rhs)` broadcasts the `(n,)` row scaling along the LAST axis instead of the first\n  (wrong values, or a shape error when `k != n`);\n- `bg[...] = ...` writes an `(n, k)` array into the `(n,)` device buffer that `_factor` allocated for the\n  solver -- this is the cupy `ValueError: Out shape is mismatched [executable_name='jit_true_divide']`.\n\nThe same is true of `post * ...` on the way back. Fix: scale with `pre[:, None]` / `post[:, None]` and solve\nthe k columns against the factorisation (one at a time, or a solver planned for an `(n, k)` right-hand side).\n\nSmallest repro (the trace + one wire network of `tests/test_peec_build_jit.py::wire_network`, `build().solve()`\non the GPU, `cudss_ffi.available = lambda: False`): raises as above. On the same network the default GPU path\n(the cuDSS custom call) and the host SuperLU callback both give Z equal to the CPU result to 1e-14, so the\ndivergence reported above needs a larger network; that is being measured separately.","files":null}]}